{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They cast pur.</b> This word is Persian, and its meaning is \"lot.\" Now this is the opposite: it is the month of Nisan. Some say that he chose to destroy Israel in the month of Adar because in it our master Moses was gathered to his people, and he did not know that in it he was born. And others said: because of the conjunction of the supernal ones in the sign of Capricorn, which is the tenth [month] counting, to the sign of Aquarius, which is the sign of Israel. But the correct interpretation is that thus it came out in his lot, for his sentence is from HaShem, and HaShem prolonged the time until Israel would repent and be saved. The nun is extra, and some say also the vav."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:52.488481312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}